#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""auto-dispatch -- one scan/dispatch pass over open wq tickets (systemd timer, every 5 min).

Automates the by-hand step "look at the open tickets and dispatch-batch them", behind
Frank's safety gates. STAGED: lumen-auto-dispatch.timer ships DISABLED; Frank approves
and enables it. Config: /home/lumen/foreman/auto-dispatch.yaml (read every pass).
Decision log (JSON lines): /home/lumen/foreman/auto-dispatch.log

Pass order (first hit ends the pass, one `halt` line logged):
  1  halt files        DISPATCH_PAUSE (Frank's kill switch), DISPATCH_DISARM (circuit-breaker
                       latch), foreman/STOP (usaged stop). Any present -> dispatch nothing.
  2  broker conflict   old foreman dispatcher armed (timer active, no latch) -> refuse; two
                       dispatchers on one queue double-spawn.
  3  budget freshness  usage data stale + on_stale=fail_closed -> halt.
  4  queue             `wq list --status open <lane>` per lane (open == unclaimed).
  5  waking hours      inside Frank's window dispatch only if queue > queue_override_threshold.
  6  concurrency       running fworker units >= max_concurrent_fworkers -> halt.
  3b failure breaker   >= N tickets dispatched <2h ago are still open (workers died/refused,
                       the Nov 5 breaker-trip pattern) -> halt until they age out or stick.
Per ticket (priority order, until free slots are used), each failure is a logged `skip`:
  lane lease held by another orchestrator | recently dispatched / daily attempt cap |
  not open or already claimed | the broker's own opt-outs, mirrored from
  dispatcher/gates.py (Frank-gate markers, [EPIC]/[DO NOT CLAIM], `wq hold`, orch-fresh grace,
  unmet `gate` path, pending decision gate) | [no-auto] | [needs-window] | unmet deps |
  model hint (default sonnet; unstamped tickets are router-assigned first) | budget floor.
NOT mirrored (broker-only, so this service is deliberately weaker there): capability preflight,
runaway, harness_defect, spawn_loop, fire gates, lane caps. fworker re-checks capability at
spawn, and the per-ticket cooldown/cap plus the failure breaker bound the damage.
Pass: `dispatch-batch <id>` (it applies its own admission gate on top of these).

Scope: Max-subscription capacity only. The per-token Anthropic API key behind
lumen/claude-* in LiteLLM is NOT a budget this script reads or spends (Frank no-spend rule).

usage: auto-dispatch [--dry-run] [--config PATH] [--verbose]
  --dry-run  decide and log to stdout; no dispatch, no router --live, no ntfy, no state writes.
exit: 0 normal (incl. halts), 1 pass had failures (also ntfy'd), 2 bad config / lock error.

PARK-AND-RESUME (wq#5009, v3). A worker that needs a decision only Frank can make parks
its round instead of holding a slot: the ticket sits in frank_gated/pending_review, which
this script never lists, so a parked ticket costs no slot, no process and no tokens. At
the top of EVERY pass -- before the halt files, because it dispatches nothing -- the pass
runs `park.py sweep` (foreman/harness/park.py): it routes Frank's answer onto the card and
reopens the ticket. A ticket whose round is ANSWERED is a RESUME of an existing session,
not a new dispatch, so it:
  - goes first in the candidate order,
  - is exempt from the redispatch cooldown and the per-day attempt cap,
  - is not counted by the failure breaker as "dispatched and still open",
  - is dispatched even inside Frank's waking hours with a small queue (he just answered).
Halt files, broker conflict, budget, concurrency and every per-ticket gate still apply.
park_resume.enabled: false turns the hook off. A sweep error is logged, never fatal.
"""
